# Linux CLI Basics

## Overview

This room introduces the fundamentals of the Linux Command Line Interface (CLI) and demonstrates how to interact with a Linux system using the terminal. It covers essential commands for navigating the filesystem, managing files and directories, inspecting system information, and performing everyday Linux tasks.

## Objectives

- Understand the purpose of the Linux Command Line Interface.
- Learn how to navigate the Linux filesystem.
- Manage files and directories using terminal commands.
- Search for files and inspect their contents.
- Become familiar with the most common Linux CLI commands.

## Skills Learned

- Linux command-line navigation
- File and directory management
- Filesystem exploration
- Reading and inspecting text files
- Basic Linux system interaction
- Terminal productivity

## Tools Used

- TryHackMe Learning Platform
- Linux Terminal (Bash)

## Key Commands

```bash
pwd
ls
ls -la
cd
mkdir
touch
cp
mv
rm
cat
less
head
tail
find
echo
clear
history
```

## Key Takeaways

- The Linux command line provides a fast and efficient way to interact with the operating system.
- Understanding the Linux filesystem is fundamental for system administration and cybersecurity.
- Essential commands such as `pwd`, `ls`, `cd`, `cat`, and `find` are used daily by Linux users and security professionals.
- The terminal makes it possible to inspect configuration files, manage directories, and troubleshoot systems effectively.
- Building confidence with the CLI creates a strong foundation for advanced Linux, scripting, and cybersecurity topics.

## Reflection

This room helped me become comfortable using the Linux terminal and introduced the essential commands required to work efficiently in a Linux environment. These foundational skills will support my learning in system administration, penetration testing, digital forensics, and other cybersecurity disciplines.

